Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:30:25 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/18] fix(desktop): Overview wording follows policy, source
 and split

Findings from an adversarial review of the data-driven Overview, each
reproduced before fixing:

- The footnote claimed "baseline detection policy, no ISO 15118 rule arms"
  in every edition. It is now built from summary.detectionPolicy (absent =
  baseline; otherwise it names the ISO 15118-2 rules and SLAC mode), followed
  by a separate sentence on how the research panel relates to it.
- On the web and the legacy launcher the fault-mix card said it was read
  from "this edition's data/summary.json". The source clause now follows
  `desktop`, and the unseen-stations claim is dropped when the summary has no
  station count. Neutral "benchmark above" wording replaces "this edition" in
  the research chips, which were also wrong off the desktop.
- "not this edition's 41ded2cdd5c2ba3f" read as if the id were this
  edition's; the id now sits with "earlier model set".
- The research-model check returns "unknown" when the sidecar artifact and
  the leaderboard fingerprint disagree (models and summary packaged from
  different runs), and never fingerprints a rule-armed benchmark against the
  baseline arm.
- The ISO-reviewed profile matched a summary that kept the 295 inconclusive
  sessions as clean; profile matching now requires faulty, clean and scored
  counts to agree.
- In-sample training stations (1.3.0 byStationTrain) are filtered off the
  held-out station cards even if the page merges them into `stations`.
- NO_POWER_DELIVERED text covers sessions that closed before PreCharge
  (9 of 360 in v4); hero chip reads "Held-out fault families" so it no longer
  clashes with the guide's catalog count; the Test-sessions card says "full
  held-out set" instead of "full fleet"; the station dialog names Agentic AI
  as the model behind its per-station score.

Tests: 16 files / 284 pass; tsc has no errors under fault-detection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
